      {"path": "{out}/t_zscore_matrix.h5", "format": "h5", "class": "E2"}
    ],
    "threads_arg": "--numberOfProcessors",
    "memory": {"budget_mb": 108},
    "large": true,
    "notes": "The designated validation input: 11,104 restriction fragment bins of chromosome X with float64 values from 0.170 to 1914.015, so the bins are inhomogeneous and fit_cut_intervals snaps every start to a multiple of the 1,843 bp median. It also calls 378 boundaries, the largest set in the corpus for this tool. It is the case that found the one real numeric difference in the port: hicmatrix materialises the z-score band by adding a sparse band of ones and subtracting one again, so every float64 value is round tripped through v + 1 - 1 and loses its lowest bits. Computing from v directly left the z-scores 5.4e-11 relative away from the reference, which passes ED but is not E2; reproducing the round trip makes them bit identical."
  },
