    "notes": "--TAD_sep_score_prefix, which no Python test passes. The spectrum and the z-score matrix are read from the committed reference rather than recomputed, so this case exercises only the calling half: peakdetect, delta_wrt_window, the Wilcoxon rank sum p-values and the uncorrected threshold. It is also the richest call set in the corpus, 1,407 boundaries and 1,402 domains. Budget is 2.2 * W of the z-score matrix plus 64 MB, W being 36.0 MB."
